            <ArticleTitle>[Epidural abscess associated with epidural block in a patient with immunosuppressive disease].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>506-8</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A patient with myeloproliferative disorders and diabetes mellitus received epidural block twice for treatment of the low back and leg pain. The drugs used were 1% mepivacaine 4 ml for the first and 1% mepivacaine 6 ml and dexamethazone 4 mg for the second on the next day. Epidural abscess was noticed 2 days later when pus was aspirated through a block needle. MRI revealed the abscess localized at L5/S1. Intensive treatment including epidural drainage and antibiotics succeeded in healing the abscess. Use of epidural block for immunocompromized patients should be decided carefully.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
